WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:04.560
Clarence Gilyard Jr. appeared in some&nbsp;
of the biggest action movies of the 80s,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:09.720
only to walk away from acting to become a beloved&nbsp;
professor. In the wake of his tragic passing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:12.480
let's take a look back at his&nbsp;
remarkable life and career.

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:17.952
"You know what, I don't even go by "junior"&nbsp;
anymore. I'm 63 years old, good heavens."

00:00:17.952 --> 00:00:24.660
Die Hard actor, author, and university professor&nbsp;
Clarence Gilyard passed away at the age of 66 due&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:30.600
to an unspecified illness on November 28, 2022.&nbsp;
Born into a military family on December 24,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:35.280
1955, Gilyard, the son of U.S. Air&nbsp;
Force Officer Clarence Gilyard Sr.,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:40.080
initially attended the United States Air Force&nbsp;
Academy himself for a year before landing on his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:45.840
true passion. He found success through roles in&nbsp;
not only Die Hard but also Top Gun and Walker,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:51.060
Texas Ranger, but Gilyard semi-retired from&nbsp;
acting in 2005 to teach at the University&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.060 --> 00:00:56.400
of Nevada Las Vegas' College of Fine Arts.&nbsp;
UNLV's Dean Nancy Uscher said in a statement:

00:01:12.120 --> 00:01:19.140
Gilyard had 37 acting credits and managed to&nbsp;
win two awards. His most famous roles included&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:23.460
the over-the-top computer hacker Theo in&nbsp;
Die Hard, Lieutenant Junior Grade Marcus&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.460 --> 00:01:28.500
"Sundown" Williams in Top Gun, and private&nbsp;
investigator Conrad McMasters on Matlock.

00:01:28.500 --> 00:01:33.415
"I was also Santa Claus's elf at a Sears."

00:01:33.415 --> 00:01:38.880
In an interview with getTV, Gilyard credited&nbsp;
Matlock star Andy Griffith as one of his mentors,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:42.420
someone who taught him how to be funny&nbsp;
on-screen. GIlyard told the outlet:

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:58.320
After Matlock, Gilyard landed&nbsp;
one of his most well-known roles,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.320 --> 00:02:03.300
playing Ranger James Trivette on Walker,&nbsp;
Texas, Ranger. When asked by why Walker,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:07.020
Texas Ranger is still popular to&nbsp;
this day, Gilyard replied to getTV,

00:02:23.540 --> 00:02:27.734
"And here you are." "Here I&nbsp;
am, wearing a silver star."

00:02:27.734 --> 00:02:33.420
From teaching film to playing pilots, priests,&nbsp;
cowboys, and computer-literate thieves,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.420 --> 00:02:39.180
Gilyard was a versatile, knowledgeable, and&nbsp;
compassionate individual. In his personal life,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.180 --> 00:02:44.280
Clarence Gilyard Jr. was a devout Roman Catholic.&nbsp;
He told the story of his conversion to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:50.880
Catholic News Agency in 2016. In 1995, Gilyard&nbsp;
hit rock bottom while living a hard-partying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.880 --> 00:02:56.460
lifestyle. Then, he crossed paths with a man&nbsp;
who invited him to Mass. It was a life-changing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.460 --> 00:03:01.200
experience for Gilyard. Gilyard's faith led&nbsp;
him to appear in the first two Left Behind&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:05.820
movies, Left Behind and Left Behind II:&nbsp;
Tribulation Force, as Pastor Bruce Barnes.

00:03:05.820 --> 00:03:10.320
After Walker: Texas Ranger, Gilyard&nbsp;
took a break from acting in 2006 to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.320 --> 00:03:14.040
become an associate professor of film and&nbsp;
theater at the University of Las Vegas,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:17.700
Nevada. Gilyard told the Las&nbsp;
